movable","kind":"file","line":10},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh","kind":"file","line":379},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Every changed file maps to a requirement: the remove.theme row at row level, the helper by an exact file-level trace","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z is in review.changes (added, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-theme-removable","default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc:remove.theme"],"scenario":"in a live session with one extra theme, remove it with omarchy theme remove from a terminal, open the menu and press Enter on Remove > Theme within 0.5 s: the row may still show from the previous answer and Enter only closes the menu"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The menu re-runs the guards on each open but first draws the previous answers, about 0.5 s on a reference machine, as for every guarded row (docs/menu.md, Guards). Removing the last theme from a terminal and opening Remove at once can still show Theme until the batch lands; Enter then runs the remover, which says nothing and exits. Before any answer (the first open of a session) the row shows too: the mirror's pre-answer witness checks that isVisible keeps the guarded row with no answer applied, and that the batch then answers remove.theme:w:0 for an empty home. The PR and 390Z state this window; whether a maintainer wants a narrower one is a product question for all guarded rows, not this row.","refs":[{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":296},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh","kind":"file","line":442},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: the first open after the last extra theme goes away, or the first open of a session, can still show the row for about half a second","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Open Remove right after removing the last extra theme\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"The engine reads Implements: annotations in .jsonc files. This PR edits default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc, so the baseline's trace review of STK-REQ-260922-XTNR (the menu, file-level on that file) does not cover this tree. The proof work re-reviews both links with citations: XTNR -> the file, and SW-REQ-261003-390Z -> the remove.theme row (line 295 annotation). The package lists XTNR under traceReviewRestamped, the suspect_clean gate passed (unchanged from the base), and no suspect trace link remains. These are proof records, not part of the upstream change.","refs":[{"id":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":2},{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":295},{"id":"suspect_clean","kind":"check"}],"severity":"info","title":"The mirror carries its own reviewed trace records for both .jsonc links, since this PR changes the menu definition","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"The PR replaces one expression in the remover: `find ~/.config/omarchy/themes -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -xtype l -printf '%f\\n'`. It listed every non-symlink directory directly under the folder, dot-directories included; it did not descend 